    "com.scaleway.search_v1alpha1#SearchV1alpha1": {
      "type": "service",
      "version": "v1alpha1",
      "operations": [
        {
          "target": "com.scaleway.search_v1alpha1#SearchResources"
        }
      ],
      "traits": {
        "smithy.api#title": "Search API",
        "smithy.api#documentation": "The Scaleway Search API enables you to locate products and resources across an organization.\n\n**Search by**:\n\n- Product name or resource type\n- Resource ID\n- Resource name\n\n**Returned metadata**:\n\n- Resource location\n- Associated project (name and ID)\n- Creation and last modified date\n\n## Concepts\n\nRefer to the [Organizations and Projects - Glossary](https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/organizations-and-projects/concepts/glossary/), or [Use the Resource Explorer](https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/organizations-and-projects/project/use-resource-explorer/) to find definitions and information on all Search API related terminology.\n\n## Quickstart\n\nNote that the Search is also integrated in the [Scaleway CLI](https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/cli). Refer to [scw search](https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/cli/search) in CLI documentation for more details.\n\n<Message type=\"requirement\">\n- You have a [Scaleway account](https://console.scaleway.com/)\n- You have created an [API key](https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/iam/how-to/create-api-keys/) and that the API key has sufficient [IAM permissions](https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/iam/reference-content/permission-sets/) to perform the actions described on this page\n- You have [installed `curl`](https://curl.se/download.html)\n</Message>\n\n1. Configure your environment variables:\n\n   <Message type=\"note\">\n   This is an optional step that seeks to simplify your usage of the Search API.\n   </Message>\n\n    ```bash\n    export SCW_SECRET_KEY=\"<YOUR_API_SECRET_KEY>\"\n    export SCW_ORGANIZATION_ID=\"<YOUR_ORGANIZATION_ID>\"\n    ```\n\n2. Run the following command to perform a basic search query and get the list of the resources attached to your organization:\n\n    ```bash\n    curl -X GET \\\n        -H \"X-Auth-Token: $SCW_SECRET_KEY\" \\\n        \"https://api.scaleway.com/search/v1alpha1/resources?organization_id=$SCW_ORGANIZATION_ID\"\n    ```\n\n   Example response:\n\n    ```json\n    {\n    \"resources\": [\n        {\n        \"id\": \"0dac255c-83e7-483a-895c-73a6e1bdaca4\",\n        \"name\": \"my-cpu-instance-example\",\n        \"organization_id\": \"13280ed3-afff-4abc-9a8c-eb972589c821\",\n        \"project_id\": \"13270ed5-afff-4abc-8a7c-eb972389c821\",\n        \"type\": \"sbs_volume\",\n        \"zone\": \"fr-par-1\",\n        \"created_at\": \"2026-10-09T11:54:21.593179Z\",\n        \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-09T11:54:22.438089Z\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"next_page_token\": \"\"\n    }\n    ```\n\n## Technical information\n\n### Availability Zones / Regions\n\nScaleway Search API is a global service. It can search for Scaleway products and resources on whatever locality (zone, region or global as well) they are in.\n\n## Technical limitations\n\nRefer to the [Resource explorer - Supported resource types](https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/organizations-and-projects/project/use-resource-explorer/#supported-resource-types) documentation for the complete list of resources supported by the Search API.\n\n## Going further\n\nFor more help using Scaleway Search API, check out the following resources:\n\n- The [`search` CLI documentation](https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/cli/search#documentation-for-scw-search)\n- Scaleway [main documentation](https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/)\n- The [Slack Community](https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/tutorials/scaleway-slack-community/)\n- The Scaleway [support ticketing system](https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/account/how-to/open-a-support-ticket/)."
      }
    }
  }
